{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# CNNs \u2014 LeNet to ResNet Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: LeNet-5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A minimal, faithful LeNet. Tanh activations, average pooling. The only concession to modernity is that we use `nn.CrossEntropyLoss` downstream instead of the original Gaussian connections."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class LeNet5(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_classes=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(1, 6, kernel_size=5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(6, 16, kernel_size=5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.pool = nn.AvgPool2d(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(16 * 5 * 5, 120)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(120, 84)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(84, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.pool(torch.tanh(self.conv1(x)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.pool(torch.tanh(self.conv2(x)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.flatten(x, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.tanh(self.fc1(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = torch.tanh(self.fc2(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.fc3(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = LeNet5()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 1, 32, 32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {net(x).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Expected output: `output: torch.Size([1, 10])`, `params: 61,706`. That is the entire digit classifier that started modern vision."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: A VGG block"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One reusable block: two 3x3 convs, ReLU, batch norm, max pool."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class VGGBlock(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, out_c):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(in_c, out_c, kernel_size=3, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bn1 = nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(out_c, out_c, kernel_size=3, padding=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bn2 = nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.pool = nn.MaxPool2d(2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = F.relu(self.bn1(self.conv1(x)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = F.relu(self.bn2(self.conv2(x)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.pool(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class MiniVGG(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_classes=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.stack = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            VGGBlock(3, 32),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            VGGBlock(32, 64),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            VGGBlock(64, 128),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Flatten(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(128, num_classes),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(self.stack(x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = MiniVGG()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 3, 32, 32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {net(x).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three VGG blocks on CIFAR-sized input, an adaptive pool, one linear layer. ~290k parameters. Plenty for CIFAR-10."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: A ResNet BasicBlock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core building block of ResNet-18 and ResNet-34."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class BasicBlock(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, in_c, out_c, stride=1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv1 = nn.Conv2d(in_c, out_c, kernel_size=3, stride=stride, padding=1, bias=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bn1 = nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conv2 = nn.Conv2d(out_c, out_c, kernel_size=3, stride=1, padding=1, bias=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.bn2 = nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if stride != 1 or in_c != out_c:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.shortcut = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                nn.Conv2d(in_c, out_c, kernel_size=1, stride=stride, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                nn.BatchNorm2d(out_c),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.shortcut = nn.Identity()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = F.relu(self.bn1(self.conv1(x)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = self.bn2(self.conv2(out))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = out + self.shortcut(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return F.relu(out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`bias=False` on conv layers is a batch-norm convention \u2014 BN's beta parameter already handles the bias, so carrying conv bias as well is a waste. The `shortcut` only needs a real conv when stride or channel count changes; otherwise it is a no-op identity."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: A tiny ResNet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Stack four groups of BasicBlocks to get a working ResNet for CIFAR-sized inputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class TinyResNet(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_classes=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.stem = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(3, 32, kernel_size=3, stride=1, padding=1, bias=False),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.BatchNorm2d(32),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.layer1 = self._make_group(32, 32, num_blocks=2, stride=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.layer2 = self._make_group(32, 64, num_blocks=2, stride=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.layer3 = self._make_group(64, 128, num_blocks=2, stride=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.layer4 = self._make_group(128, 256, num_blocks=2, stride=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Flatten(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Linear(256, num_classes),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _make_group(self, in_c, out_c, num_blocks, stride):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        blocks = [BasicBlock(in_c, out_c, stride=stride)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(num_blocks - 1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            blocks.append(BasicBlock(out_c, out_c, stride=1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return nn.Sequential(*blocks)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.stem(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.layer1(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.layer2(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.layer3(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = self.layer4(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "net = TinyResNet()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 3, 32, 32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"output: {net(x).shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"params: {sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters()):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Four groups of two blocks each. Stride 2 at the start of groups 2, 3, 4. Channel count doubles at every downsample. Roughly 2.8M parameters. That is the standard recipe that scales cleanly up to ResNet-152."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Compare parameter-to-feature efficiency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run the same input through all three networks and compare parameter counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def summary(name, net, x):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    y = net(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"{name:12s}  input {tuple(x.shape)} -> output {tuple(y.shape)}  params {params:>10,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "x = torch.randn(1, 3, 32, 32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "summary(\"LeNet5\",     LeNet5(),       torch.randn(1, 1, 32, 32))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "summary(\"MiniVGG\",    MiniVGG(),      x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "summary(\"TinyResNet\", TinyResNet(),   x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three models, three eras, three orders of magnitude in parameter count. For CIFAR-10 accuracy, you need roughly: LeNet 60%, MiniVGG 89%, TinyResNet 93% after a few epochs of training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Count parameters by hand for `TinyResNet` layer by layer. Compare against `sum(p.numel() for p in net.parameters())`. Where does the majority of the parameter budget go \u2014 convs, BN, or the classifier head?\n2. **(Medium)** Implement the Bottleneck block (1x1 -> 3x3 -> 1x1 with skip) and use it to build a ResNet-50-style network for CIFAR. Compare params against `TinyResNet`.\n3. **(Hard)** Remove the skip connection from `BasicBlock`, train a 34-block \"plain\" network and a 34-block ResNet on CIFAR-10 for 10 epochs each. Plot training loss vs epoch for both. Reproduce the He et al. Figure 1 result where the plain deep network converges to higher loss than its shallower twin."
      ]
    }
  ],
